<Project>

  <!--
    Deployment campaign Stage C1 — one place that says what build this is.

    Ruling 12 requires every commissioning report to be stamped with machine id, Canary
    version and tier. Machine id shipped 2026-08-18. This file supplies the version, and it
    exists because there was NO version anywhere: no <Version>, no AssemblyVersion, no
    InformationalVersion in any csproj, and nothing in the CLI reporting one. A QC report
    that cannot say which build produced it is the same identity gap that made environment
    captures undiffable before machine identity was added.

    The SDK already stamps AssemblyInformationalVersion as "<Version>+<git sha>" when
    SourceLink or the default git integration is present, so declaring Version here yields
    version AND the exact commit at runtime with no extra machinery. CanaryVersion reads it
    back; see src/Canary.Core/CanaryVersion.cs.

    Deliberately NOT set here: TargetFramework, Nullable, ImplicitUsings,
    TreatWarningsAsErrors. Those differ per project on purpose - the Agent multi-targets
    net8.0;net48 and the Rhino agent is net48 only - and hoisting them would silently change
    what those projects compile against.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Version>0.9.0</Version>
    <Product>Canary</Product>
    <Company>Canary</Company>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
